---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Quiet Compass" description="The Quiet Compass principles: calm wayfinding, semantic motion, progressive enhancement, and experimentation as punctuation." element="earth" route="C03">
  <section data-route-section data-element="earth" data-bearing="170">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal><div><span class="route">C03 / ABOUT</span><h1>Advanced underneath. Quiet on the surface.</h1></div><p>Quiet Compass is a behavioral design system: movement means direction, lines mean relationships, the compass means orientation, elements establish environment, and typography establishes voice.</p></div>
      <div class="bento-grid">
        <article class="bento wide" data-reveal><span class="route">01 / PRINCIPLE</span><h2>Experimentation behaves like punctuation.</h2><p>It should add emphasis, timing, and personality without interrupting reading or navigation.</p></article>
        <article class="bento" data-reveal><span class="route">02 / ACCESS</span><h2>Progressive by default.</h2><p>Semantic HTML works first. Motion, filtering, search, prefetching, personalization and richer media layer on only when supported.</p></article>
        <article class="bento" data-reveal><span class="route">03 / PERFORMANCE</span><h2>Presence without weight.</h2><p>Static generation, selective hydration, modern images, delayed activation and explicit performance budgets keep the experience responsive.</p></article>
        <article class="bento wide" data-reveal><span class="route">04 / SYSTEM</span><h2>Five elements, one grammar.</h2><p>Water supports analysis and navigation. Wood supports development and process. Earth supports context and rest. Metal supports precision. Fire marks consequential action.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>